  "- Mandatory Step 0 pre-flight check for regional Google Cloud MCP servers (e.g. Dataproc) before using MCP tools or falling back to gcloud/bq CLI. Use whenever interacting with Dataproc clusters, Spark batches, jobs, sessions, or regional GCP resources. Fixes regional MCP servers whose endpoint URL still has an unreplaced $GCP_REGION / ${REGION} placeholder across Claude Code, Codex, and Antigravity. Trigger: an expected mcp__*_{service}_* tool is missing entirely (not just failing), or a call to one fails/hangs on a malformed host. Check via ToolSearch/deferred-tools listing before falling back to gcloud/bq CLI. Asks the user for a region, patches the live MCP config file(s), and tells the user how to restart without losing session context.": "\u533a\u57df\u7ea7 Google Cloud MCP \u670d\u52a1\uff08\u5982 Dataproc\uff09\u8fde\u63a5\u914d\u7f6e\u4fee\u590d\uff1a\u81ea\u52a8\u68c0\u6d4b\u5e76\u66ff\u6362\u672a\u89e3\u6790\u7684 $GCP_REGION \u5360\u4f4d\u7b26\uff0c\u4fee\u590d MCP \u5de5\u5177\u8fde\u63a5\u62a5\u9519\u3002",
  "Mandatory Step 0 pre-flight check for regional Google Cloud MCP servers (e.g. Dataproc) before using MCP tools or falling back to gcloud/bq CLI. Use whenever interacting with Dataproc clusters, Spark batches, jobs, sessions, or regional GCP resources. Fixes regional MCP servers whose endpoint URL still has an unreplaced $GCP_REGION / ${REGION} placeholder across Claude Code, Codex, and Antigravity. Trigger: an expected mcp__*_{service}_* tool is missing entirely (not just failing), or a call to one fails/hangs on a malformed host. Check via ToolSearch/deferred-tools listing before falling back to gcloud/bq CLI. Asks the user for a region, patches the live MCP config file(s), and tells the user how to restart without losing session context.": "\u533a\u57df\u7ea7 Google Cloud MCP \u670d\u52a1\uff08\u5982 Dataproc\uff09\u8fde\u63a5\u914d\u7f6e\u4fee\u590d\uff1a\u81ea\u52a8\u68c0\u6d4b\u5e76\u66ff\u6362\u672a\u89e3\u6790\u7684 $GCP_REGION \u5360\u4f4d\u7b26\uff0c\u4fee\u590d MCP \u5de5\u5177\u8fde\u63a5\u62a5\u9519\u3002",
